## Development

This project uses [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) for environment management and [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/) for dependency management.

### Setup

1. Install uv (if not already installed):
```bash
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
```

2. Create a virtual environment:
```bash
uv venv
```

3. Activate the virtual environment:
```bash
# On Unix/macOS
source .venv/bin/activate

# On Windows
.venv\Scripts\activate
```

4. Install dependencies:
```bash
uv pip install poetry
poetry install
```

### Development Tools

This project uses the following development tools:

- **ruff**: Linting and formatting
- **mypy**: Type checking
- **pytest**: Testing
- **lefthook**: Git hooks for pre-commit checks

Install lefthook:
```bash
# On macOS
brew install lefthook

# On Linux
curl -1sLf 'https://dl.cloudsmith.io/public/evilmartians/lefthook/setup.rpm.sh' | sudo -E bash
sudo yum install lefthook

# Or using go
go install github.com/evilmartians/lefthook@latest
```

Initialize git hooks:
```bash
lefthook install
```

### Running Tests

```bash
pytest
```

### Running Linting and Type Checks

```bash
# Format code
ruff format .

# Lint code
ruff check .

# Type check
mypy src/{{ project_name }}
```

Or run all checks at once:
```bash
./scripts/build.sh
```

{% if enable_agent_harness %}## Agent harness

This project ships an agent harness: maintainability checks that run only on new and changed
code, so agents (and people) fix what they touch without being pushed into codebase-wide
refactors.

```bash
./scripts/check.sh            # gate on code changed since the merge-base
./scripts/check.sh --all      # whole-codebase audit, report only
./scripts/check.sh --mutation # mutation testing on changed lines (slow)
./scripts/hotspots.sh         # churn x complexity report
```

`AGENTS.md` is the guide for coding agents. See [docs/agent-harness.md](docs/agent-harness.md)
for how the checks work and how to tune them.

